# L §4.3 rule 2: "a later version that gives it a dated row makes such a reader state `at` (LOAD-LAWDATE)".
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "a source"

input n: int

def m2: int = n + 1

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  n = 2

version v2
  cite s
  governs 2026-06..
  known 2026-05-01
  replace n = 3

ask q1: m2
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LAWDATE ...
